Subject: [PATCH] CMake: Increase minimum CMake version to 3.16

Backported from upstream commits 67b2e8155 ("Increase minimum CMake version
to 3.16") and 1df8ab3d2 ("CMake: indicate compatibility up to CMake 4.0"),
squashed: 1.1.1 declares a 3.3 minimum, and CMake 4 refuses to configure any
project asking for less than 3.5, so the build dies before it starts.  The
upper bound of the range is what upstream settled on and keeps policy
behaviour pinned where 1.1.1 expects it.

Upstream: https://github.com/selmf/unarr/commit/67b2e8155bc03d9189ea6c52baf13f67f2a739f8
          https://github.com/selmf/unarr/commit/1df8ab3d281409e9fe6bed8bf485976bb47f5bef
Applies-to: all environments
---
diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index f38b229..a7a0e3a 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.3 FATAL_ERROR)
+cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.16...4.0 FATAL_ERROR)
 
 project(
   unarr
